# The project's bytes are entirely LF — verified at HEAD (zero CRLF sequences, zero bare CR
# across every committed text file). On Windows, `core.autocrlf=true` used to rewrite working
# copies to CRLF, which silently broke every LF-needle witness in `check.sh`
# (qa-a11y-witness.mjs, qa-locale-wiring-witness.mjs), making the local definition of done
# unrunnable on the host every developer this arc uses. `text=auto` classifies by content,
# so binaries are untouched; `eol=lf` pins the LF this repository has always used.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Pre-generated artefacts are treated as binary by `text=auto` only when git's heuristic agrees,
# and their bytes are published hashes — pin them so a merge driver can never helpfully normalize
# them into a different digest.
docs/api/openapi.json -text
*.png -text
*.jpg -text
*.jpeg -text
*.gif -text
*.ico -text
*.pdf -text
*.zip -text
*.jar -text
*.class -text
